WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.021
Zann leaped to his feet.

2
00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:17.924
"Where?" "Come, I'll show you!"

3
00:00:18.664 --> 00:00:20.506
The nomad was already rushing out again.

4
00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:28.092
When Zann and his friends burst out of the cave, the nomad was whistling for the hoof beasts,

5
00:00:28.453 --> 00:00:29.934
which were still grazing nearby.

6
00:00:30.754 --> 00:00:32.256
Several of the beasts trotted over.

7
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.442
"Did you find both Gliss and Wyssa, or just one of them?"

8
00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:39.484
Perda asked as she climbed onto one of the hoof beasts.

9
00:00:39.504 --> 00:00:44.127
"I'm not sure," the nomad messenger admitted.

10
00:00:44.147 --> 00:00:48.310
"My group of searchers was nearing an area where there are several deep caves.

11
00:00:48.911 --> 00:00:51.172
Ripples of magic energy were coming from that direction.

12
00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:53.634
We assumed it was coming from your friends.

13
00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:56.476
The others continued on while I returned to fetch you."

14
00:00:57.336 --> 00:00:59.638
"Are you sure it wasn't Morb sending out the energy?"

15
00:00:59.998 --> 00:01:00.599
Zann asked.

16
00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:02.460
The messenger grimaced.

17
00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:03.901
"Quite sure.

18
00:01:04.561 --> 00:01:06.923
We saw him atop the Seeing Stone when we passed.

19
00:01:07.524 --> 00:01:08.785
Luckily he didn't notice us."

20
00:01:10.506 --> 00:01:15.050
Soon Zann, Perda, Darb, and several nomads were galloping across the desert.

21
00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:17.952
The messenger led them to some rocky hills.

22
00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:22.916
Two nomads were crouched by a large, dark hole in the side of a big hill.

23
00:01:24.037 --> 00:01:26.719
One of them turned when she heard Zann and the others coming.

24
00:01:27.539 --> 00:01:28.680
Her face was ashen.

25
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.662
"She's in trouble!"

26
00:01:30.942 --> 00:01:31.823
the nomad called.

27
00:01:32.343 --> 00:01:38.002
"Hurry!" Zann jumped off his hoof beast and ran to the mouth of the cave.

28
00:01:38.943 --> 00:01:40.704
He gasped when he looked inside.

29
00:01:41.504 --> 00:01:44.386
Just inside the cave was a deep, wide pit.

30
00:01:45.106 --> 00:01:47.347
Looking down, Zann saw Wyssa.

31
00:01:48.328 --> 00:01:50.269
She was standing on a huge boulder.

32
00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:55.592
All around her, filling every bit of the floor, were hundreds of cave hissers!

33
00:01:56.572 --> 00:01:58.493
Zann felt his blood run cold.

34
00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:03.276
Cave hissers were among the most dangerous creatures in all of Magica.

35
00:02:04.544 --> 00:02:08.865
They lived underground, and their bite could immobilize even a large dragon.

36
00:02:08.885 --> 00:02:10.146
"Oh, no!"

37
00:02:10.546 --> 00:02:12.746
Perda cried as she knelt beside Zann.

38
00:02:12.766 --> 00:02:15.107
"Can those hissers reach her?"

39
00:02:15.127 --> 00:02:18.108
"Not quite," a nomad said grimly.

40
00:02:18.128 --> 00:02:20.148
"But she can't reach us either."

41
00:02:20.168 --> 00:02:22.949
"Why can't she just levitate out?"

42
00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:23.849
Perda said.

43
00:02:23.869 --> 00:02:27.791
"Or magically immobilize the hissers so she can get by?"

44
00:02:28.751 --> 00:02:30.111
Wyssa had heard them by now.

45
00:02:30.951 --> 00:02:32.832
She squinted up at Perda with a frown.

46
00:02:33.672 --> 00:02:37.776
"I tried both those things, but my magic isn't working," she snapped.

47
00:02:37.796 --> 00:02:41.039
"Do you have any other brilliant ideas, girl?"

48
00:02:41.779 --> 00:02:45.663
"The lower half of this cave seems to be a natural vacuum," a nomad said.

49
00:02:46.503 --> 00:02:48.205
Now Zann understood the problem.

50
00:02:48.945 --> 00:02:50.927
Magic didn't work in a vacuum.

51
00:02:51.768 --> 00:02:53.209
Wyssa was still staring up at them.

52
00:02:53.229 --> 00:02:59.114
"If I had all of my potions and ingredients, I could blast these hissers into oblivion."

53
00:03:00.095 --> 00:03:00.796
Zann nodded.

54
00:03:01.568 --> 00:03:04.430
Wyssa came from a world with little natural magic.

55
00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:09.272
Her people had learned to combine various ingredients to create magic energy.

56
00:03:10.113 --> 00:03:13.875
Once she'd even managed to open a wormhole in a world with no magic at all!

57
00:03:13.895 --> 00:03:17.677
"Maybe we can find the ingredients you need," Zann said.

58
00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.838
A nomad cleared her throat.

59
00:03:19.858 --> 00:03:22.520
"I don't think there will be time for that."

60
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:23.460
She pointed.

61
00:03:24.461 --> 00:03:26.842
The cave hissers were piling atop one another.

62
00:03:26.862 --> 00:03:28.803
"What are they doing?"

63
00:03:29.203 --> 00:03:29.864
Zann asked.

64
00:03:30.668 --> 00:03:32.770
"They're forming a pyramid," Darb said.

65
00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:37.695
"I've heard that hissers will cooperate with one another to reach—" He gulped.

66
00:03:37.715 --> 00:03:40.757
"Food." Zann gulped too.

67
00:03:41.338 --> 00:03:43.680
They didn't have time to look for magical ingredients.

68
00:03:44.361 --> 00:03:48.745
If they didn't figure out how to get Wyssa out of there soon, she would become the cave

69
00:03:48.785 --> 00:03:49.626
hissers' lunch!

70
00:03:50.646 --> 00:03:52.828
He glanced around, desperate for ideas.

71
00:03:53.589 --> 00:03:56.312
His gaze fell on the hoof beasts standing nearby.

72
00:03:57.128 --> 00:04:00.991
A couple of them had the nomads' long lassoes looped around their necks.

73
00:04:01.971 --> 00:04:02.312
"I know!"

74
00:04:02.732 --> 00:04:03.412
Zann exclaimed.

75
00:04:03.432 --> 00:04:05.834
"We can pull Wyssa out with your ropes!

76
00:04:06.114 --> 00:04:07.035
They're strong enough, right?"

77
00:04:07.795 --> 00:04:08.696
A nomad nodded.

78
00:04:09.396 --> 00:04:10.357
"Strong enough, yes.

79
00:04:10.977 --> 00:04:12.018
But not long enough."

80
00:04:12.959 --> 00:04:13.539
"That's okay."

81
00:04:14.179 --> 00:04:15.821
Zann grabbed a couple of the lassoes.

82
00:04:15.841 --> 00:04:17.462
"We'll tie them together."

83
00:04:18.562 --> 00:04:21.264
Soon the lassoes formed one long rope.

84
00:04:21.965 --> 00:04:26.648
But when Zann tried to toss it to Wyssa, he couldn't get it to land anywhere near her.

85
00:04:27.424 --> 00:04:29.566
Wyssa was too far away from the cave mouth.

86
00:04:30.287 --> 00:04:33.169
A couple of the nomads tried too, but it was no use.

87
00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:36.692
The end of the rope kept falling onto the hissers.

88
00:04:37.533 --> 00:04:41.817
On one try, a hisser clung to the rope, and the nomad struggled to shake it off.

89
00:04:41.837 --> 00:04:43.979
"This isn't working!"

90
00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:44.920
Perda cried.

91
00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.661
"We need a new plan."

92
00:04:47.822 --> 00:04:48.823
Zann bit his lip.

93
00:04:49.604 --> 00:04:52.326
How could they get the end of the rope out to Wyssa?

94
00:04:53.007 --> 00:04:54.068
He studied the cave.

95
00:04:54.876 --> 00:04:57.898
A large stalactite hung down right above the pit.

96
00:04:57.918 --> 00:05:02.561
"If I could get out there and hang on, I could lower the rope to Wyssa," he said,

97
00:05:02.781 --> 00:05:03.421
thinking aloud.

98
00:05:03.441 --> 00:05:06.163
"Then the rest of you could pull us both out."

99
00:05:06.963 --> 00:05:09.384
"What?" Darb looked out at the stalactite.

100
00:05:10.485 --> 00:05:11.726
"How are you going to get there?"

101
00:05:12.586 --> 00:05:13.327
Zann shrugged.

102
00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.548
"I think I can jump that far."

103
00:05:16.609 --> 00:05:17.649
Perda looked alarmed.

104
00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.410
"What if you miss?"

105
00:05:20.351 --> 00:05:22.072
Zann tied the rope around his waist.

106
00:05:22.892 --> 00:05:26.354
"I'll keep the rope short enough so that if I do miss, I can't fall all the way

107
00:05:26.394 --> 00:05:29.555
down." "It seems dangerous," a nomad argued.

108
00:05:29.575 --> 00:05:31.316
"There must be another way."

109
00:05:32.176 --> 00:05:36.918
Zann glanced down just in time to see Wyssa kick a cave hisser off the top of the

110
00:05:36.978 --> 00:05:39.679
boulder. Others were creeping toward her feet.

111
00:05:40.759 --> 00:05:42.260
"There's no time," Zann said.

112
00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.341
"I'll be fine."

113
00:05:44.121 --> 00:05:46.582
The others tied their end of the rope to a sturdy rock.

114
00:05:47.362 --> 00:05:51.204
Zann took a deep breath, trying to gauge the distance out to the stalactite.

115
00:05:51.928 --> 00:05:52.649
Could he do this?

116
00:05:54.049 --> 00:05:55.711
He took a running start and leaped.

117
00:05:57.552 --> 00:05:58.853
He reached the stalactite.

118
00:05:58.873 --> 00:06:00.354
"I did it!"

119
00:06:00.594 --> 00:06:01.034
he cried.

120
00:06:01.054 --> 00:06:04.356
"I—" Suddenly he felt his grip slipping.

121
00:06:05.157 --> 00:06:09.059
He began to slide downward and clawed furiously at the slippery rock.

122
00:06:09.079 --> 00:06:12.582
"Levitate!" he cried without thinking.

123
00:06:12.602 --> 00:06:15.304
"Zann, no magic!"

124
00:06:15.544 --> 00:06:16.164
Perda yelled.

125
00:06:17.005 --> 00:06:17.885
It was too late.

126
00:06:18.746 --> 00:06:21.748
Zann's magic energy bounced against the vacuum below.
